  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile models with avgpool are currently strongest, and scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 under the same setting, while image-only evidence is weak. The key remaining uncertainty on the RNA side is whether the untested scgpt encoder can improve on scvi_n200 when profile setting and aggregation are held at their currently best values. config_008 tests this single-factor representation comparison, isolating encoder choice without adding image or fusion complexity. Under a limited budget, this exploits the strong multiprofile/avgpool evidence while efficiently exploring an important design choice before moving to more complex multimodal configurations."
